import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse('{"title":"Test Framework in Handl (handl-packages/test), Delete plugin-lib-test — design detail","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Test Framework in Handl (`handl-packages/test`), Delete `plugin-lib-test` — design detail","type":"design","date":"2026-09-05T00:00:00.000Z","updated":"2026-10-29T00:00:00.000Z","refs":["ADR-0092"]},"headers":[],"relativePath":"handl/project/design/0092-test-framework-in-handl.md","filePath":"vendored/handl/project/design/0092-test-framework-in-handl.md"}'),a={name:`handl/project/design/0092-test-framework-in-handl.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="adr-0092-test-framework-in-handl-handl-packages-test-delete-plugin-lib-test-—-design-detail" tabindex="-1">ADR-0092: Test Framework in Handl (<code>handl-packages/test</code>), Delete <code>plugin-lib-test</code> — design detail <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0092-test-framework-in-handl-handl-packages-test-delete-plugin-lib-test-—-design-detail" aria-label="Permalink to “ADR-0092: Test Framework in Handl (handl-packages/test), Delete plugin-lib-test — design detail”">​</a></h1><p>Moved verbatim from ADR-0092 (ADR-0161 size budget). The ADR carries the rules; this page carries the mechanism, tables and rationale.</p><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to “Context”">​</a></h2><p>Today <code>plugin-lib-test</code> is one crate hosting <strong>two unrelated concerns</strong>:</p><ol><li><strong>The framework library</strong> — <code>assert.rs</code>, <code>property.rs</code>, <code>benchmark.rs</code>, <code>fuzz.rs</code>, <code>snapshot.rs</code>, <code>test.rs</code>, plus the <code>test.hnl</code> op/handl wiring (<code>OpRegistry</code>, <code>HandlModule</code>s, <code>TestLibraryPlugin</code>). This is the handl-callable API: <code>assert.equal</code>, <code>property.for_all</code>, <code>snapshot.match</code>, etc.</li><li><strong>The runner</strong> — <code>runner.rs</code> (discovery, execution, reporting).</li></ol><p>ADR-0089 extracts the runner into <code>plugin-engine-test</code>. This ADR migrates the <strong>framework library</strong> to handl under <code>handl-packages/test/</code> and <strong>deletes <code>plugin-lib-test</code></strong>.</p><p>The framework is already <em>declared</em> in handl: <code>handl-packages/test/test.hnl</code> declares the <code>op</code> interface (<code>assert.equal : (Value, Value) -&gt; Bool</code>, …) and binds each op to a Rust handl (<code>handl &quot;assert.equal&quot; = rust_assert_equal</code>). The Rust modules implement those handls and register them in an <code>OpRegistry</code>. This is exactly the Phase 1 <code>op</code>/<code>handl</code> form ADR-0077 describes for the stdlib migration: the contract is handl, the implementation is Rust. ADR-0077&#39;s program is to replace the Rust handls with pure-handl implementations and drop the Rust bridge.</p><p>The framework library is <strong>pure logic</strong> in almost all cases:</p><ul><li><code>assert.*</code> — value equality, containment, boolean checks, thrown-error capture. All expressible in handl over <code>Value</code>.</li><li><code>snapshot.format</code> — pretty-print a value to JSON. Expressible in handl once a JSON serializer exists in the stdlib.</li><li><code>property.for_all</code> — run a function with a seeded RNG for N iterations. Needs a deterministic RNG primitive; the iteration/compare logic is pure handl.</li><li><code>benchmark.run</code> — timing. <strong>Not pure</strong>: needs a clock primitive. Stays a thin FFI handl until a <code>time.now</code> primitive lands in the stdlib, then moves to handl.</li><li><code>fuzz.run</code> — like <code>property.for_all</code> but failure-collecting. Same RNG dependency.</li><li><code>test.run</code> — run a suite and return a report. Pure handl over the result types.</li></ul><p>So the migration is almost entirely pure-handl; the only FFI dependencies are a seeded RNG primitive (for <code>property</code>/<code>fuzz</code>) and a clock primitive (for <code>benchmark</code>). Both are stdlib concerns, not framework concerns.</p><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision”">​</a></h2><p>Migrate the test framework library from <code>plugin-lib-test</code> (Rust) to <strong>pure handl under <code>handl-packages/test/</code></strong>, following the ADR-0077 <code>op</code>/<code>handl</code> → pure-handl program. Then <strong>delete <code>plugin-lib-test</code></strong>.</p><h3 id="target-layout" tabindex="-1">Target layout <a class="header-anchor" href="#target-layout" aria-label="Permalink to “Target layout”">​</a></h3><div class="language-"><button title="Copy code" data-copied="Copied" class="copy"></button><span class="lang"></span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes handl-dark github-light" style="--shiki-dark:#ffffff;--shiki-light:#24292e;--shiki-dark-bg:#2a2a2a;--shiki-light-bg:#fff;" tabindex="0" dir="ltr"><code><span class="line"><span>handl-packages/test/</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    test.hnl         -- op declarations + cap declarations (already exists)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    assert.hnl       -- pure-handl assert.* implementations</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    property.hnl     -- pure-handl property.for_all (over an RNG primitive)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    fuzz.hnl         -- pure-handl fuzz.run (over an RNG primitive)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    snapshot.hnl     -- pure-handl snapshot.format / snapshot.match</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    benchmark.hnl    -- handl over a clock primitive until time.* lands</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    test.hnl         -- pure-handl test.run (suite → report)</span></span>
<span class="line"><span>    docs/            -- (already exists)</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Each <code>op</code> keeps its declared signature; only the <code>handl &quot;...&quot; = rust_*</code> binding is replaced by a pure-handl definition (or, for <code>benchmark</code>/RNG cases, by a handl to a stdlib FFI primitive).</p><h3 id="migration-per-op" tabindex="-1">Migration per op <a class="header-anchor" href="#migration-per-op" aria-label="Permalink to “Migration per op”">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Op</th><th>Now</th><th>After</th><th>FFI dependency</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>assert.equal</code> / <code>not_equal</code> / <code>true</code> / <code>false</code> / <code>contains</code> / <code>throws</code></td><td>Rust handl</td><td>pure handl</td><td>none</td></tr><tr><td><code>snapshot.format</code> / <code>snapshot.match</code></td><td>Rust handl</td><td>pure handl</td><td>a stdlib JSON serializer</td></tr><tr><td><code>property.for_all</code></td><td>Rust handl</td><td>pure handl</td><td>a seeded RNG primitive (<code>random.*</code> in stdlib)</td></tr><tr><td><code>fuzz.run</code></td><td>Rust handl</td><td>pure handl</td><td>same seeded RNG primitive</td></tr><tr><td><code>test.run</code></td><td>Rust handl</td><td>pure handl</td><td>none</td></tr><tr><td><code>benchmark.run</code></td><td>Rust handl</td><td>handl over <code>time.now</code></td><td>a clock primitive (<code>time.*</code> in stdlib)</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Ops with an FFI dependency land as handl-over-primitive the moment the primitive exists; until then they stay as Rust handls <em>in the runner crate</em> (<code>plugin-engine-test</code>) as a temporary bridge, not in a resurrected <code>plugin-lib-test</code>.</p><h3 id="crate-boundary" tabindex="-1">Crate boundary <a class="header-anchor" href="#crate-boundary" aria-label="Permalink to “Crate boundary”">​</a></h3><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Crate</th><th>Before</th><th>After</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>plugin-lib-test</code></td><td>Framework library + runner</td><td><strong>Deleted</strong></td></tr><tr><td><code>plugin-engine-test</code> (ADR-0089)</td><td>—</td><td>Runner only; may carry temporary Rust handls for <code>benchmark</code>/RNG until stdlib primitives land</td></tr><tr><td><code>handl-packages/test/</code></td><td><code>test.hnl</code> (op declarations)</td><td>Full pure-handl framework library</td></tr></tbody></table><h3 id="relationship-to-adr-0089" tabindex="-1">Relationship to ADR-0089 <a class="header-anchor" href="#relationship-to-adr-0089" aria-label="Permalink to “Relationship to ADR-0089”">​</a></h3><p>ADR-0089 extracts the runner into <code>plugin-engine-test</code> <strong>first</strong>. This ADR then migrates the framework library to handl and deletes <code>plugin-lib-test</code>. The ordering matters: the runner must have a home before the framework&#39;s old home is removed. The runner consumes the framework via the handl module chain regardless of whether the framework is the Rust or the handl implementation, so the migration is transparent to the runner.</p><h3 id="relationship-to-adr-0077" tabindex="-1">Relationship to ADR-0077 <a class="header-anchor" href="#relationship-to-adr-0077" aria-label="Permalink to “Relationship to ADR-0077”">​</a></h3><p>This is a direct instance of ADR-0077&#39;s stdlib-migration program (<code>op</code>/<code>handl</code> Phase 1 → pure-handl). The test framework is a stdlib library like any other; it is not special. The only reason it has its own ADR is the coupled crate deletion (<code>plugin-lib-test</code>) and the FFI dependencies (RNG, clock) that gate two of the ops.</p><h3 id="what-stays-rust" tabindex="-1">What stays Rust <a class="header-anchor" href="#what-stays-rust" aria-label="Permalink to “What stays Rust”">​</a></h3><ul><li>The <strong>runner</strong> (<code>plugin-engine-test</code>) — ADR-0089, stays Rust per ADR-0085 rule 6.</li><li><strong>Temporary Rust handls</strong> for <code>benchmark.run</code> (clock) and <code>property.for_all</code>/<code>fuzz.run</code> (seeded RNG) <em>if</em> those stdlib primitives don&#39;t exist yet. These live in <code>plugin-engine-test</code> as stopgaps, <strong>not</strong> in a recreated <code>plugin-lib-test</code>. They are deleted the moment the primitives land.</li></ul><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequences”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong><code>plugin-lib-test</code> is deleted.</strong> The runner-framework tangle is gone. The runner is <code>plugin-engine-test</code> (Rust); the framework is <code>handl-packages/test/</code> (handl).</li><li><strong>The test framework is written in handl, from day one of the migration.</strong> This matches ADR-0077&#39;s direction and means the framework is type-checked, linted, and formatted by the same tooling as all other handl code.</li><li><strong>Two ops gate on stdlib primitives</strong> (seeded RNG, clock). Until those land, <code>benchmark</code>/<code>property</code>/<code>fuzz</code> use temporary Rust handls hosted in <code>plugin-engine-test</code>. This is an explicit, tracked stopgap — not a permanent split.</li><li><strong>The <code>op</code> signatures in <code>test.hnl</code> are the stable contract.</strong> Migrating an op from Rust-handl to pure-handl changes only the <code>handl &quot;...&quot; = …</code> binding; callers see no difference.</li><li><strong>No grammar change.</strong> The framework is handl code using existing surface syntax; the <code>test</code> <em>keyword</em> (test declarations) is a separate concern owned by ADR-0089&#39;s test-language fragment.</li></ul><h2 id="prerequisites" tabindex="-1">Prerequisites <a class="header-anchor" href="#prerequisites" aria-label="Permalink to “Prerequisites”">​</a></h2><ol><li><strong>ADR-0089 lands first</strong> — <code>plugin-engine-test</code> exists and the runner is extracted out of <code>plugin-lib-test</code>.</li><li><strong>A stdlib JSON serializer</strong> for <code>snapshot.format</code> (likely already present or near-term per ADR-0077).</li><li><strong>A seeded RNG primitive</strong> in the stdlib (<code>random.*</code>) for <code>property.for_all</code> / <code>fuzz.run</code>.</li><li><strong>A clock primitive</strong> in the stdlib (<code>time.*</code>) for <code>benchmark.run</code>.</li></ol><p>Items 3 and 4 are now satisfied: <code>rand.seeded_*</code> RNG ops and <code>time.instant_ns</code> are wired into the canonical module chain. The <code>error.raise</code>/<code>error.try</code> primitives were not needed for the framework; the pure-handl implementation uses the <strong>result pattern</strong> only (<code>{&quot;__tag__&quot;:&quot;ok&quot;,...}</code> / <code>{&quot;__tag__&quot;:&quot;err&quot;,...}</code>).</p>`,31)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};